         <div type="bio">
            <p>English writer. She and <name type="person" key="rodk94">John Rodker</name> were married in 1918 and in 1919 founded the Ovid Press, which published limited editions of works by <name type="person" key="poun85">Pound</name>, <name type="person" key="elio88">Eliot</name>, <name type="person" key="lewi82">Lewis</name>, and other modernists. They separated in 1920 when she became involved with Scottish writer and critic <name type="person">Cecil Maitland</name>. Butts became a prolific and wide-ranging author. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
